Sprint 3 BATCH 7 — IDOR mutation test evidence
==============================================

Target: server/services/wellnessService.ts upsertTodayEntry SELECT-existing.

Original code (load-bearing IDOR clause on the WHERE):
    const [existing] = await db
      .select()
      .from(dailyWellnessLog)
      .where(and(eq(dailyWellnessLog.userId, userId), eq(dailyWellnessLog.date, today)))
      .limit(1);

Mutation (remove the userId clause):
    const [existing] = await db
      .select()
      .from(dailyWellnessLog)
      .where(and(eq(dailyWellnessLog.date, today)))
      .limit(1);

Test invoked:
    npx vitest run server/test/routes/wellness.test.ts \
      -t "primary IDOR mutation target"

Result with mutation applied:
    FAIL  server/test/routes/wellness.test.ts > POST /api/wellness/log
    > issues SELECT-existing with eq(dailyWellnessLog.userId, callerId)
    > — primary IDOR mutation target

    AssertionError: Expected eq(<column>, "user-A") in WHERE clause.
      Got eq calls: ["2026-05-06","user-A","user-A","user-A","user-A","user-A"]
      expected undefined to be defined

    Test Files: 1 failed (1)
    Tests:      1 failed | 20 skipped (21)

The remaining "user-A" eq() calls land on the OTHER columns hit during the
same request (userGamification.userId for streak read + state + UPDATE,
users.id for audit-log email lookup). The column-aware
expectOwnershipClause(dailyWellnessLog.userId, "user-A") correctly detects
that none of them is on dailyWellnessLog.userId — the IDOR ownership clause
that was removed.

Result after reverting the mutation:
    PASS  server/test/routes/wellness.test.ts (21 tests)
    Test Files: 1 passed (1)
    Tests:      1 passed | 20 skipped (21)

Final full suite (after revert):
    Test Files:  16 passed | 1 failed (17 — pre-existing aiService)
    Tests:       324 passed | 15 failed (339 — 15 pre-existing aiService)

